{
  "chapter": "reliability/fallbacks-and-breakers",
  "tier": "drill",
  "notes": [
    "The ladder is walked in order. A rung whose breaker is open is skipped without being",
    "called — failing fast is the whole point of the open state. A rung that may not serve",
    "this risk tier is skipped too.",
    "Only a transient failure falls through to the next rung. A refusal or a malformed",
    "request halts the ladder: falling back on the first is shopping for a provider that",
    "will comply, and falling back on the second just fails again somewhere else.",
    "Every served response records which rung answered and whether it was degraded. Without",
    "that field silent degradation is undetectable in principle, not merely in practice.",
    "An exhausted ladder is an escalation, not a 500. Handing the work to a person is a",
    "correct outcome, and it is the rung that never depends on someone else's capacity."
  ],
  "ladder": [
    { "name": "primary", "maxTier": 2 },
    { "name": "primary-alt-region", "maxTier": 2 },
    { "name": "reduced-scope", "maxTier": 2 },
    { "name": "smaller-model", "maxTier": 0 },
    { "name": "secondary-provider", "maxTier": 0 },
    { "name": "human-queue", "maxTier": 3 }
  ],
